      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "After testing it some further, it seems that the values are actually reset at some point, but not immediately after leaving the world. Instead, the global shader variable values seem to be reset some time after leaving the world after the one which the variable was declared in.\nI initially tested this using Kilerbomb's \"AudioOrbs\" world since they added a global float called \"_UdonIsAudioOrbs\", which is set to 1 as soon as it loads in. I wrote a quick shader to test this new feature, and the shader becomes completely white if \"_UdonIsAudioOrbs\" is 1, otherwise it would be normal.\nUsing a local avatar at first, I was able to see that the value was 1, even after leaving the world. But now I've also went ahead to try the shader with a regular avatar, and the issue remained.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
